#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ferry-dash — a live local dashboard for the ferry LAN AI relay.

Serves an auto-refreshing web page (default http://localhost:8091) for the
litellm route proxy that `ferry up --route` runs. It shows:

  * ferry UP/DOWN + host/port + served model groups
  * the orchestrator topology (primary + strict fallback chain) from litellm.yaml
  * the gemini worker pool
  * recent request activity parsed from the proxy log (rate, status, clients)
  * an on-demand "Test backends" probe (the ONLY thing that spends tokens)

Auto-refresh costs nothing: it reads the local proxy log plus litellm's
/health/liveliness and /v1/models (no model calls). Standard library only, so
it runs under any python3 on macOS and Linux — no venv, no pip.

Usage:
  ferry-dash                 # serve on http://localhost:8091
  ferry-dash --open          # ...and open it in your browser
  ferry-dash --port 9000 --ferry http://127.0.0.1:8090
"""
